# Generated at runtime, never committed by hand
.run/
*.local.mjs

# Node
node_modules/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# The agent's own scratch. Payloads and prose are artifacts in CI; locally they
# land here so a dry run does not dirty the working tree.
.run/payload.json
.run/prose.md
.run/answer.md

# Session metadata for the AI assistant that helped build this. Kept on disk,
# deliberately not shipped: it is a working log, not part of the template.
.workbuddy-ai/

# Internal review output — engineering-assurance reports. Kept on disk for the
# maintainer, deliberately not shipped: they name the people who produced them
# and discuss this repository's own deployment posture, which is exactly the
# material the pre-publication audit exists to keep out of a public tree. The
# audit cannot see them, so `git add -A` would publish them.
deliverables/

# Design archaeology — the pre-code feasibility report and the architecture
# review. Kept on disk for the maintainer, deliberately not shipped: the report
# is a study of the harness this template was derived from, and the review
# enumerates the design's own open findings.
#
# Both were tracked from the initial commit until a history rewrite dropped them,
# so they are absent from every commit and not merely from HEAD. `.gitignore`
# governs untracked paths, and both are untracked now, which is what keeps them
# that way. Committing either again takes `git add -f`.
REPORT.md
ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md
